{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand one to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","isActive":true},{"text":" and a denial stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being a bare 403: the guard mints a fresh permission ticket for the pair the caller lacked and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches it to the thrown ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true},{"text":", so the framework adapter can return it as a header and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a UMA-aware client knows where to go for authority instead of only being told “no”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in, and deliberately so.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Emitting a challenge means minting a credential — a wire call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the Protection API, and a live ticket, produced on a path the caller did not explicitly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. A guard that did that on every denial by default would turn each unauthorized request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into a Protection API call, which is a denial-of-service amplifier pointed at your own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authorization server. So it happens only where an application asked for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failure is not escalation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" If minting fails — the PAT expired, the Protection API is down,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the resource declares none of the requested scopes — the denial still surfaces as an ordinary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" without a challenge. A caller who was going to be refused is refused either way;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letting a Protection API outage turn a deny into a 503 would hand the outage a second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consequence, and letting it turn into an allow would be a security bug."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"title":"UmaChallenger","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/pat":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pat","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV","text":"Sensitive","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Protection API Token: a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"client-credentials"}]},{"type":"text","text":" token carrying the "},{"code":"uma_protection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" scope"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(§20.2 rule 1). A user token cannot stand in — a minted ticket is bound to the "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that minted it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/pat","role":"symbol","title":"pat","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/asURI":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/asuri","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"asURI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The authorization server the caller should redeem the ticket at — normally this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deployment’s issuer, read from "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/umaDiscover()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than concatenated by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand, for the same reason §12.3 rule 6 gives."}],"title":"asURI"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","title":"AxiamSDK","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger":{"title":"UmaChallenger","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A configured ","type":"text"},{"code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/init(realm:asURI:pat:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"realm"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"asURI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"pat"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV","text":"Sensitive"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}],"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/init(realm:asuri:pat:)","role":"symbol","title":"init(realm:asURI:pat:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AuthzError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AuthzError"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/authzerror","title":"AuthzError","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AuthzError"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Authorization failure (§2). Carries a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"text":" and, when the server provided them,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the denied ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"action"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resourceID"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamGuards/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamguards\/requireaccess(_:resource:scope:umachallenge:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"requireAccess","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resource","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scope","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","ki